nodecode-gemini-media is a rewrite of bytecakelake's bytecakelake/hermes-gemini-media-generation:

  https://github.com/bytecakelake/hermes-gemini-media-generation
  commit 44bc2dd0349c08cecdcb44333b9fa0000ef01d95
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 bytecakelake (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's two generation calls are here as three tools and one slash
command in Common Lisp. The rewritten source carries the same Gemini API calls the plugin made
through the google-genai SDK (model, input parts, response_format with aspect_ratio, image_size,
resolution and duration, and generation_config.video_config.task), the same aspect, size,
resolution and duration rules and the same "adjusted" flags they raise, the same curated model
table and the same id-based classifier behind the model list, the same reference-picture rules
(header sniffing for PNG, JPEG, WebP, HEIC and HEIF, 15 MB each and 18 MB together, private
hosts refused, at most 14 pictures for an image and 6 for a video), and the same error classes,
status hints and key scrubbing.

What was left out, and why: the google-genai SDK, because the cell speaks the API's HTTP
directly; Hermes's image_generate and video_generate lanes with their picker, because a
Nodecode cell declares its own tools and section; the 24-hour model-list cache on disk, because
the cell keeps the list in memory for a day and falls back to the curated table; the wall-clock
deadline on an abandoned worker thread, because NLK:HTTP's timeout is the cell's ceiling; the
MP4-only duration read above 64 MB; and Hermes's own generated-media folder, replaced by the
operator's output_dir.
